  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Ever since the update to Unity 2018 pickups, especially gravity-based ones, have had very glitchy collision. Frequently after spending an hour or two in an instance. The game will randomly start lagging to about 5 frames a second and you can see all of the pickups in the world teleporting around like crazy. Probably the easiest place to experience this glitch is in the great pug. lately instances of it don't seem to last more than an hour before one of these glitches occur causing a majority of players in the i nstance to crash\nI've managed to survive through it a few times and it can last anywhere between 5 seconds to 3 minutes from my experience\nthis is not someone exploiting a client as I've been able to reproduce this issue in an invite only instance by myself. \nThis issue has also been the cause of my own world falsely being marked as poor-performing in it's analytics page. disabling gravity and enabling kinematic on almost all the pickups in my world seems to have pretty much solved the issue\nCollision triggers also seem to have some type of rapid-fire now. For example in my own world I have a working xylophone. whenever you hit one of the bars it plays the note once and shouldn't play again until you move the mallet off of it and hit it again. But ever since the 2018 update. The trigger will rapid fire causing it to play the xylophone sample over and over\nEven one quick tap will result in the audio being played somewhere around ten times in very quick succession",
